WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.160
INFERIVA for agent networks and mobile wallets: an overview.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:09.979
Your customers rarely come to you. They go to an agent: a kiosk, a shop,

00:00:09.979 --> 00:00:13.053
a market stall. Every agent acts in your name,

00:00:13.053 --> 00:00:16.729
and every transaction is small enough to look ordinary.

00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:23.589
Monitoring designed for bank accounts sees thousands of small deposits and finds nothing.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:27.865
The risk sits in patterns across agents, wallets and time of day.

00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:31.656
INFERIVA starts with the network itself.

00:00:31.656 --> 00:00:35.841
Every agent and super agent is on record, with its location,

00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:38.352
its status and its daily cash limit.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:43.763
Detection scenarios are written for agent networks: volume spikes,

00:00:43.763 --> 00:00:47.704
round trips through the same agent, structuring across agents,

00:00:47.704 --> 00:00:50.565
and dormant wallets that suddenly move money.

00:00:50.565 --> 00:00:53.108
Each threshold is tuned to your network.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.933
Each alert shows why it fired: the rule,

00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:01.540
the agent's behaviour against its own baseline, and against its peers.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.765
So an analyst can see the one agent that changed.

00:01:05.967 --> 00:01:08.750
For fraud, a transaction is scored as it happens,

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.987
and can be stepped up or stopped before the money leaves,

00:01:11.987 --> 00:01:14.259
with every factor in the decision shown.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:19.180
Fraud and anti-money laundering look at the same customer.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:24.109
A fraud alert shows the customer's money laundering risk, and any open cases.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.590
When a report is needed, it is drafted from the case, approved and filed,

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:32.411
and tracked until the regulator acknowledges it.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.729
Every agent, every alert, every fraud decision and every report, on one record.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:43.404
So when the regulator asks about one agent, the answer is already there.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.271
To see it for your institution, talk to INFERIVA.
